From: numcodecs contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Copy the leftover bytes when bit-unshuffling a version 2 block

A Blosc1 (format version 2) block whose element count is a multiple of 8
stores the bytes that do not fill a whole element after the shuffled part.
The reader skipped them, so chunks written by C-Blosc 1.x with a typesize
that does not divide the block size were decoded with garbage at the end.
---
diff -ruN a/blosc/shuffle.c b/blosc/shuffle.c
--- a/blosc/shuffle.c
+++ b/blosc/shuffle.c
@@ -498,6 +498,9 @@
         BLOSC_TRACE_ERROR("the impossible happened: the bitunshuffle filter failed!");
         return ret;
       }
+      /* Copy the leftovers, as Blosc1 does */
+      size_t offset = size * typesize;
+      memcpy((uint8_t *) dest + offset, (const uint8_t *) src + offset, blocksize - offset);
     }
     else {
       memcpy(dest, src, blocksize);
